<!-- OUR STORY -->
<section style="padding: 4rem 1.5rem; background: #FFFFFF;">
  <div style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <h2 style="color: #1B2A4A; font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; text-align: center;">Our Story</h2>
    <div style="width: 60px; height: 3px; background: #C9A24B; margin: 0 auto 2rem auto;"></div>
    
    <p style="color: #555; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.9; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      Annada Qur'an &amp; Science Academy was established in <strong style="color: #1B2A4A;">2018</strong> in Kudan, Kaduna State, Nigeria, with a vision to bridge the gap between traditional Islamic education and modern scientific learning.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color: #555; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.9; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      We recognized that Muslim children in our community needed an institution that would nurture them in the memorization and deep understanding of the Holy Qur'an while simultaneously giving them a rigorous foundation in science, mathematics, and modern education — preparing them for both this world and the Hereafter.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color: #555; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.9;">
      Today, Annada Academy stands as a beacon of integrated Islamic education in Kaduna State, producing graduates equipped with strong faith, sound character, and academic excellence.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

